{
 "encounter_id": "00805",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Hello. I've been told my potassium's high, after the new tablet, and to come and see you. I'm trying to remember what the new tablet is."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let's go through your medicines. What's the new one?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Ramipril, 2.5 mg, once a day. It's for my kidneys. And the old one is the amlodipine, 5 mg."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How have you been since starting the ramipril?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Tired. And my legs are a bit weak, and my heart skips. Not often."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "When did you start it? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Three weeks ago. Or four. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any muscle weakness, tingling, or palpitations that scare you?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, nothing frightening. No tingling."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any vomiting, or diarrhoea, any fluid loss?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Remind me of your health background."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Chronic kidney disease, diabetes, and high blood pressure."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Do you take any supplements, salt substitute, or anti-inflammatory painkillers? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I use a low-salt substitute, because of my blood pressure. And ibuprofen, now and then, for my back. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's important. Salt substitutes contain potassium, and ibuprofen can harm the kidneys. Let me check you. Pulse, pressure. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 66 and regular, blood pressure 132 over 78, temperature 36.6, oxygen 98 percent.",
   "pause": 12.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Fine. Any breathlessness or chest tightness?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, none."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Your potassium was 5.9, and normal is up to 5.0. It's likely the ramipril, plus the salt substitute, on top of kidney disease. I'd say this is a raised potassium caused by the new tablet and the salt substitute."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is it dangerous? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "At 5.9, it needs attention. Above 6.5 it can affect the heart. So I'd like to stop the salt substitute straight away, and avoid the ibuprofen completely."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'll throw it out. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And I'm going to ask you to stop the ramipril for now, until we recheck the potassium."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'll have the nurse take a repeat blood test today."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Eat a normal diet, but go easy on bananas, oranges and potatoes for now."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I eat a banana every day. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Leave it a few days. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to see you again in a week, with the result and a plan."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A week. Thank you. ~"
  }
 ],
